{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average (arithmetic mean) age of a group consisting of doctors and lawyers in 40. If the doctors average 35 and the lawyers 50 years old, then the ratio of the numbers of doctors to the number of lawyers is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111b89f8c9e28a29f62f0509897650f28638dba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3: 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3: 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2: 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2: 1\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1: 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"470\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of doctors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the number of lawyers.  The average age of the doctors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the sum of the doctors' ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda9a9c9ca4ad706f06e53d848c6df815bdc8d3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35d$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />.  The average age of the lawyers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the sum of the lawyers' ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d3166def6bbb930b5f88d602eba25b0c292072a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50l$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" />.  With the two information, we can write an equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/8251598b3f225d7a72a5e59261d16cc60067d37b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{35d+50l}{d+l} = 40\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b7f9bd60ab390b0f40e260ed881ff74eac7496.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[35d+50l=40d+40l\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4adcb8524d14ef363063bdba0945667b1d2d91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10l=5d\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf459536e694d98609b8b4ccbd418f73a261d1b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d}{l} = 2\\]\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />\nThe ratio of the number of doctors to the number of lawyers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d8d3e0cfe44634d1190bed4e483c78137978e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2: 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"80\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" styl